cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "T-saur: a content-addressed, agent-first archive format and archiver"
message: "If you refer to T-saur in a publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bondari
    given-names: Iulian
repository-code: "https://github.com/iulianbondari/t-saur"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
version: 1.0.0-rc.1
date-released: "2026-09-24"
abstract: >-
  T-saur (.tsr) is a free, open-source archive format and archiver: content-defined chunking with
  BLAKE3 identities, container-aware and per-block compression, offline recovery volumes with
  Reed-Solomon parity, optional authenticated encryption and signatures, and read-without-extract
  operations with a Model Context Protocol server for AI agents. Version 1.0.0-rc.1 freezes format
  version 1.
keywords:
  - archive format
  - compression
  - content-addressed storage
  - erasure coding
  - AI agents
